# Allowlist: the image needs only the package sources, the build manifest (and the README and
# LICENSE it references), the lockfile, and the documentation with its menu (rendered by the
# `docs` stage). Everything else — .git, .claude/, .todos/,
# .devcontainer/, tests/, CLAUDE.md, ... — never enters the build context.
*
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!README.md
!LICENSE
!src/
!documentation/
!.config/mkdocs/mkdocs.yml

# Re-excluded inside the allowlisted tree: secrets and regenerated Python artefacts.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/id_rsa*
**/id_ed25519*
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.venv/
